wer of the Wendigo  inside Church is too strong and the cat  makes his way back to the family home  deliberately luring Ali into the road in  front of a speeding truck and jumping  out of the way to safety just before it  crashes into her the change in le is  even more noticeable initially after she  returns from the dead she's unsure where  she is but quickly understands  she's changed and she says to Lewis I'm  dead aren't I she also tells him that  she can hear the woods inside her  another indication that the wendigo  spirit has invaded and occupied her body  the demon also gives her an unnatural  physical strength that a nine year old  girl would be unlikely to possess such  as being able to drag her mother's body  all the way to the burial ground by  herself and when she fights her father  he finds it extremely difficult to  overpower her on top of that the  wendi-go can manipulate Ellie's body to  communicate and taunt the victim she's  about to kill when she attacks jerd  Ellie tells him how she saw his dead  wife Norma burning in hell and then the  Wendigo even transforms Ellie's body and  voice momentarily into Norma the  possessed Ellie does the same with her  mother Rachel first she blames her  mother for leaving her to die in the  road and then accuses her of having done  the same with her sister Zelda like Jett  he refuses to believe he's seeing the  real Norma Rachel tells Ally you're not  my daughter to which the now possessed  Ally replies then go be with her at  which point she stabs Rachel once more  there's an interesting similarity  between how the Wendigo exerts an evil  influence on people in Pet Sematary and  how Pennywise influences people to  commit terrible deeds and ears on top of  that there's a deliberate Easter Egg to  Stephen King's it with a road sign for  dairy in the scene where Rachel engages  stuck in a traffic jam as they try to  get back to Ludlow dairy is of course  the town in Maine where it takes place  and where Pennywise shows up every 27  years in contrast to it though where the  losers Club is able to band together to  defeat the evil spirit Pet Sematary has  a much darker ending in fact the 2019  remake goes further perhaps in the 1989  movie or the original novel in terms of  how many of the Creed family are killed  by the Wendigo in this version Ellie is  first killed by the truck Ellie then  kills her mother and resurrects her and  then as Lewis fights with Ellie the  reanimated Rachel comes out of nowhere  and mortally Spears Lewis through the  back after they drag his body off to the  Mi'kmaq burial ground we cut to a  chilling final scene of gage helplessly  waiting in the family car outside their  home Lewis Ellie and Rachel then appear  walking towards the car and Church jumps  menacingly interview  and as the screen cuts to black there's  a horrifying sound of the car doors  unlocking if you have any doubt about  whether gage survived there's actually a  clue in the opening scene of the movie  which heavily implies that he didn't the  scene shows the aftermath after the car  door was unlocked the doors been opened  and there are a couple of bloody  handprints on the window plus some blood  inside the door  it seems pretty likely then that the  possessed bodies of the crude family  will have killed gage and dragged him  off to bury and resurrect him providing  the evil Wendigo demon with yet another  corpse to inhabit however in the  original story it's just gage and Rachel  who were killed and they're both buried  by Lewis and resurrected and in the 1989  movie Rachel also kills Lewis after she  returns there's also a couple of other  major characters we need to talk about  first of all the Zelda Rachel sister who  has a terrifying part to play in the  remake and gets more screen time than in  the 1989 movie we learn in the film that  Zelda suffered from spinal meningitis  and is particularly scary scene where we  see just how badly she traumatized  Rachel Rachel he was left alone by her  parents to care for her sick sister used  a dumbwaiter to send up food to Zelda  but after the food got stuck Zelda died  in a horrific mangled mess when she fell  into the dumbwaiter and after Rachel and  her family moved to Ludlow it feels like  the spirit of the wendi-go that stalks  the land surrounding their new house  plays a part in soma nning the terrible  recurring visions of Zelda that Rachel  begins to suffer after the resurrected  Church returns to the house and starts  acting maliciously for example by  scratching Ellie for the first time not  only does Lewis hear a terrible groaning  sound from the basement with a warning  that the destruction of all he loves is  very near but Rachel starts to hear  terrible thumping noises from the roof  and inside the walls which culminate in  a petrifying vision of her dead sister  appearing inside the bathroom cabinet in  a similar way to how Zelda died inside  the dumbwaiter years ago  Rachel's case shows us again how the  Wendigo is able to use the grief shame  and sense of regret someone may suffer  after a terrible tragedy to manipulate  its victims psychologically and  eventually caused their downfall we also  need to talk about Victor Pascal who  plays a small but important part as a  voice he repeatedly warns Lewis again  it's the dangers of crossing the  deadfall he also tries to warn Lewis  against taking the dead Ellie up to the  burial ground though of course Lewis  ignores him and Pascale also warns gage  and Rachel that Lewis is in danger now  some people have theorized that Pascale  may not be acting so benevolently in pet  cemetery because you could argue that he  not only draws lewis's attention to the  deadfall but he also leads Rachel engage  back to Ludlow placing them in danger so  that they eventually become possessed by  the Wendigo however if we take Pascale  at face value as a caution and remember  that it was actually Jud who took Lewis  over the threshold I think that pass cow  is a character that serves to draw our  attention to the folly of ignoring the  warnings in front of us Pet Sematary  also warns us of the dangers of not  learning how to deal with grief and  tragedy appropriately for instance after  Lewis discovers Church has died Rachel  who's never been able to get over the  death of her sister Austin Lewis to tell  Ellie that her cat ran away  basically Rachel asked him to say  anything except that the cat died  likewise after Ellie dies Lewis can't  accept her death or his feelings of  guilt and regret insisting on staying in  Ludlow after both Ellie and Rachel asked  to move back to Boston so he  deliberately makes an excuse to stay  behind when Rachel engaged go to stay  with her family and he also drugs Jud so  he doesn't stop him from digging up the  dead Ellie and taking her to be  resurrected Jud who also didn't want to  see Ellie sad at the loss of Church was  the original instigator of course in  taking the dead cat to be resurrected  all of these terrible decisions show the  folly of not facing up to reality and  instead turning to superstition or  toying with supernatural forces we don't  understand I've already touched on a few  Pet Sematary book a movie Easter eggs  but there's some other interesting ones  you might have missed Ellie refers to  herself as Allie the great and terrible  both before she becomes possessed and  afterwards the nickname isn't just a  neat little bit of foreshadowing of her  terrible fate it's also an easter egg to  book Zelda who had a picture on her wall  of all the great and terrible which  smash when she died in King's novel as  the great and terrible becomes a theme  associated with an unnatural and evil  death and so of course it's especially  fitting that it's a title that Elias use  before she's taken over by the wicked  wendi-go spirit  an easter egg that flashes by pretty  quickly as when the truck driver who  accidentally kills Ali gets distracted  by a phone call from Sheena just before  the accident Sheena is a punk rocker is  the song by The Ramones that the truck  driver from the 1989 movie was playing  in his vehicle during the accident that  killed gage in fact the decision of the  filmmakers of this remake to change the  child killed and the accident did upset  some King purists you prefer the idea of  the youngest child becoming corrupted by  the wendigo and being turned into a  murderous infant for this movie though I  think it turned out to be a great change  and twist  Jesse Lawrence who plays Ali in the new  movie delivered a fantastic performance  as both the sweet-natured le before her  death and the angry murderously  possessed Ali after her resurrection  having the older child come back from  the dead also allowed her to interact  with her family in a way that just  wouldn't have been possible or realistic  with a toddler  and if you wondering whether there's  likely to be a sequel that follows on  from these events while the directors  have said they're much more interested  in a possible prequel story in an  interview with consequence of sound  producer Lorenzo de Bono Ventura said  that if there's anything here there's a  prequel if you look at the book we  didn't cover all that stuff that happens  before the Creed family moves in as he  says there are stories from kings  original book which weren't included in  this adaptation but which were included  in the 1989 movie such as how one of the  town's deceased World War two veterans  Timmy Bateman was resurrected after his  body was sent back to the town from the  war there was a tiny Easter Egg to this  in the new movie by renews paper  headline that flashes by very quickly  another area that could be explored in a  prequel is a jump further back in time  to when the Native Americans were still  in the area around Ludlow this remake  deliberately pointed out that the entire  plot of land that the Creed's  owned extended back to the pet cemetery  and beyond the barrier and when Lewis  was reading about the Wendigo in Judds  house there was a newspaper headline  that read Indian land claims still  unsettled a prequel could investigate  what part the Wendigo might have played  in any conflict over land between Native  American tribes and those who settled  the town of Ludlow now if you've seen  both movies which did you prefer tapping  the top right to vote and then you'll be  able to see the results and leave any  thoughts you have about the movie in the  comment  below if you enjoy deep dives like this  into your favorite horror films  subscribe and hit the bell to get all my  new videos tapleft but all the clues and  easter eggs you might have missed in  Jordan peels us or tap right for another  video you're sure to like thanks for  watching and see you next time you pick  a movie lovers
 

